               <rdf:li rdf:parseType="Resource">
                  <photoshop:LayerName>Bardic Inspiration</photoshop:LayerName>
                  <photoshop:LayerText>Bardic Inspiration</photoshop:LayerText>
               </rdf:li>
               <rdf:li rdf:parseType="Resource">
                  <photoshop:LayerName>1</photoshop:LayerName>
                  <photoshop:LayerText>1</photoshop:LayerText>
               </rdf:li>
               <rdf:li rdf:parseType="Resource">
                  <photoshop:LayerName>Level</photoshop:LayerName>
                  <photoshop:LayerText>Level</photoshop:LayerText>
               </rdf:li>
               <rdf:li rdf:parseType="Resource">
                  <photoshop:LayerName>You can inspire others through stirring words or music. As a  b</photoshop:LayerName>
                  <photoshop:LayerText>You can inspire others through stirring words or music. As a  bonus action on your turn choose one creature other than yourself within 60 feet of you who can hear you. That creature gains one Bardic Inspiration die. Once within the next 10 minutes, the creature can roll the die and add the number rolled to one ability check, attack roll, or saving throw it makes. You regain any expended uses of Bardic Inspiration when you finish a long rest.  At 5th level you regain all of your expended uses of Bardic Inspiration when you finish a short or long rest.</photoshop:LayerText>
               </rdf:li>
               <rdf:li rdf:parseType="Resource">
                  <photoshop:LayerName>Song of Rest</photoshop:LayerName>
                  <photoshop:LayerText>Song of Rest</photoshop:LayerText>
               </rdf:li>
               <rdf:li rdf:parseType="Resource">
                  <photoshop:LayerName>2</photoshop:LayerName>
                  <photoshop:LayerText>2</photoshop:LayerText>
               </rdf:li>
               <rdf:li rdf:parseType="Resource">
                  <photoshop:LayerName>Level copy 3</photoshop:LayerName>
                  <photoshop:LayerText>Level</photoshop:LayerText>
               </rdf:li>
               <rdf:li rdf:parseType="Resource">
                  <photoshop:LayerName>You can use soothing music or oration to help revitalize your w</photoshop:LayerName>
                  <photoshop:LayerText>You can use soothing music or oration to help revitalize your wounded allies during a short rest. If you or any friendly creatures who can hear your performance regain hit points at the end of the short rest, each of those creatures regains an extra 1d6 hit points.   The hit points regained increases to 1d8 at 9th level, to 1d10 at 13th level, and to 1d12 at 17th level.</photoshop:LayerText>
               </rdf:li>
               <rdf:li rdf:parseType="Resource">
                  <photoshop:LayerName>Bard College Feature</photoshop:LayerName>
                  <photoshop:LayerText>Bard College Feature</photoshop:LayerText>
               </rdf:li>
               <rdf:li rdf:parseType="Resource">
                  <photoshop:LayerName>3</photoshop:LayerName>
                  <photoshop:LayerText>3</photoshop:LayerText>
               </rdf:li>
               <rdf:li rdf:parseType="Resource">
                  <photoshop:LayerName>Level copy 3</photoshop:LayerName>
                  <photoshop:LayerText>Level</photoshop:LayerText>
               </rdf:li>
               <rdf:li rdf:parseType="Resource">
                  <photoshop:LayerName>Countercharm</photoshop:LayerName>
                  <photoshop:LayerText>Countercharm</photoshop:LayerText>
               </rdf:li>
               <rdf:li rdf:parseType="Resource">
                  <photoshop:LayerName>6</photoshop:LayerName>
                  <photoshop:LayerText>6</photoshop:LayerText>
               </rdf:li>
               <rdf:li rdf:parseType="Resource">
                  <photoshop:LayerName>Level copy 3</photoshop:LayerName>
                  <photoshop:LayerText>Level</photoshop:LayerText>
               </rdf:li>
               <rdf:li rdf:parseType="Resource">
                  <photoshop:LayerName>As an action, you can start a performance that lasts until the </photoshop:LayerName>
                  <photoshop:LayerText>As an action, you can start a performance that lasts until the  end of your next turn. During that time, you and any friendly creatures within 30 feet of you have advantage on saving throws against being frightened or charmed. A creature must be able to hear you to gain this benefit. The performance ends early if you are incapacitated or silenced or if you voluntarily end it (no action required).</photoshop:LayerText>
               </rdf:li>
               <rdf:li rdf:parseType="Resource">
                  <photoshop:LayerName>Bard College Feature</photoshop:LayerName>
                  <photoshop:LayerText>Bard College Feature</photoshop:LayerText>
               </rdf:li>
